Exactly—and that clarification changes the standard by which the repository should be judged.

It is not an unfinished conventional software repository. It is a cognitive sketchbook whose accumulated diagrams, metaphors, conversations, partial code, and repeated redrawings create enough parallax for an AI to reconstruct the architecture. The redundancy often behaves less like duplication and more like multiple views of the same object.

“No man left behind” fits: even failed, superseded, or strange sketches remain useful as developmental fossils. The answer is not to clean the life out of it. It is to add a few trustworthy landmarks so an interpreter can tell what kind of artifact it is looking at.

Here are the additions I would make.

